   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "brauchen … zu",
     "texto": [
      "**Brauchen** (to need) + **zu** + infinitive means \"need to do something\": **Du brauchst nicht zu kommen** (you don't need to come). With **nicht** it expresses that something is not necessary, not that it is forbidden. It is a standard and common construction.",
      "You can also use **kein**: **Du brauchst kein Brot zu kaufen** (you don't need to buy bread)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Difference with müssen",
     "texto": [
      "With **müssen** it is an obligation: **Du musst kommen** (you have to come). With **brauchen … nicht zu** it means it isn't necessary: **Du brauchst nicht zu kommen** (you don't need to come). Watch out for the false friend: **brauchen** doesn't mean \"to use\", it means \"to need\"."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Obligation",
     "columnas": [
